  "body": "In [the rules for choosing a browsing context](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-rules-for-choosing-a-browsing-context-given-a-browsing-context-name), `rel=\"noopener\"` only has an effect of putting a browsing context into a new group if the target implies a new browsing context (`_blank_ or a non-existent name).\r\n\r\nIt would be helpful for the other target types to also support `rel=\"noopener\"` such that the browsing context is swapped into a new browsing context group. This would support noopener semantics on regular link navigations, for example.\r\n\r\nRelated to https://github.com/WICG/ScrollToTextFragment/pull/70",
